       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In progress. DOH, will look at adherence of its hospitals for upgrading, renovations, and retrofitting to the eight performance standards of DOH Green and Safe Health Facilities Manual. For newly constructed facilities, hospitals will be subjected to seven performance standards considering that Governance is not applicable to these facilities. Special focus will be given to adherence to the following performance standards: Environmentally Resilient Health Facility, Site Sustainability, and Materials Sustainability to ensure that the funded facilities are built up to resilience standard. DOH, with support from the Bank, will conduct trainings for DOH assessors and implementers on Green Viability Assessment. The trainings will include a module on enhancing the structural resilience government hospitals. Information source: DOH</narrative>
